  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe playback worker calculates the full stock removal before it publishes a frame (#2181). During this time the viewport shows the uncut stock. The transport clock did not stop. The tool moved over stock that showed no cut. On a large block, the full program can play before the first cut shows. This is the \"no visible stock removal\" of #2611.\n\n- `crates/ui/src/play_precalc.rs`: new `holds_playhead` (true while `Precalc::Running`) and `advance_playhead` (the transport clock step; it does nothing while the calculation runs).\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs`: the transport uses `advance_playhead`. The scrub slider is disabled while the calculation runs. Play, Stop and Cancel still work. Cancel stops the calculation, and playback then cuts live as before.\n- `crates/app/tests/stock_play_picture.rs` (new): plays the worker as the transport does, composes each frame as the eye does (`max(mesh, cut)`), and counts the solid texels. It proves that the frames show the removal, at the full budget and at the display budget.\n- `docs/decisions/2611-playhead-waits-for-precalc.md`: the decision and the dropped options.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Without the fix, the pinning UI test fails: `the playhead waits while the stock removal is calculated`, `left: Some(0.1)`, `right: Some(0.0)`.\n- With the fix, it passes (25 s).\n- The two app tests pass on main and on this branch. Thus the data of the worker frames is correct, and the defect is the clock.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `play_precalc_tests::the_playhead_waits_for_the_calculation_and_then_the_drawn_stock_shows_the_cut` (camcraft-ui lib): FAIL before, PASS after.\n- `stock_play_picture::the_drawn_stock_shows_the_removal_as_the_program_plays` (camcraft-app): PASS.\n- `stock_play_picture::the_drawn_stock_shows_the_removal_at_the_display_budget` (camcraft-app): PASS.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`): 10 steps, 0 failed. Clippy on `camcraft-ui` and `camcraft-app` (`--all-targets -D warnings`): clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No screenshots. The change holds the playhead in time; a still picture does not show it. I did not launch the GUI.\n- The GPU eye shader was not run. The app test composes `max(mesh, cut)` on the CPU in the same way.\n- The refusal path, where the status line says \"simulation shows the uncut stock: ...\" (for example posed, rotary or lathe operations), was not examined. If the reporter sees that line, it is a different cause.\n- The issue gives no model and no steps. The reproduction uses a staged face operation on a box stock.\n\nChangelog: The stock simulation playhead now waits while the stock removal is calculated, so the tool no longer plays over stock that shows no cut.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2611\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
